# This .dockerignore uses an "allowlist" approach for security and a minimal build context.
# For more info: https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#dockerignore-file
#
# The repo root is only ever a build context for .devcontainer/Dockerfile, which copies
# nothing but the Go module files. Without this, every devcontainer build would ship
# external/ (~200MB of vendored checkouts) and frontend/node_modules to the daemon.
#
# The application images build from narrower contexts -- `docker buildx build ./auth-service`
# and `./frontend` in the Makefile -- so they are unaffected by this file. If a root-context
# build is ever added, re-include what it needs below.

# 1. Ignore everything by default.
**

# 2. Explicitly re-include only what the build COPYs.
!auth-service/go.mod
!auth-service/go.sum
